<ac:structured-macro ac:name="details"><ac:parameter ac:name="id">dbsec-platform</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><table><tbody><tr><th><p>Platform</p></th><td><p>MongoDB</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Product</p></th><td><p>MongoDB Community / Enterprise Server (replica sets, sharded clusters)</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Versions in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[e.g., 7.0, 8.0]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Policy</p></th><td><p><code>SEC-POL-DB-001</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Technical basis</p></th><td><p>CIS MongoDB 7 / 8 Benchmark</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable audit file(s)</p></th><td><p>CIS_MongoDB_*.audit (database and mongod.conf checks via Unix audit)</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable credential</p></th><td><p>Database credential, type MongoDB, plus SSH credential for mongod.conf and file checks</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Control prefix</p></th><td><p><code>MONGO</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Instances in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[count or link to CMDB]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Controls</p></th><td><p>11</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Automated (Tenable)</p></th><td><p>7 of 11</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Compliance % (last scan)</p></th><td><p>0%</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Open CRITICAL / HIGH</p></th><td><p>0</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Last Tenable scan</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Owner team</p></th><td><p><em>[Team]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Next review due</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr></tbody></table></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Company policy – SEC-POL-DB-001</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p>This page is part of the company Database Security Configuration Policy (SEC-POL-DB-001). Its requirements are mandatory for every database in scope. Deviations need an approved entry in the DB Security – Exceptions Register. CIS Benchmarks and Tenable audit files are the technical basis and assessment method; where this policy differs from CIS, this policy applies.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="toc"><ac:parameter ac:name="maxLevel">2</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>
<h2>Scope &amp; applicability</h2>
<ul><li>Apply to every mongod and mongos, including arbiters and config servers.</li><li>MongoDB Atlas: controls Atlas enforces (TLS, authentication) are N/A; project-level settings are reviewed manually.</li><li>Audit logging and native encryption at rest need Enterprise; Community deployments use the compensating controls in Comments.</li></ul>
<h2>Tenable assessment setup</h2>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Item</p></th><th><p>Value</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan template</strong></p></td><td><p>Policy Compliance Auditing (credentialed)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Audit file(s)</strong></p></td><td><p>CIS_MongoDB_*.audit (database and mongod.conf checks via Unix audit)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Credential</strong></p></td><td><p>Database credential, type MongoDB, plus SSH credential for mongod.conf and file checks</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan account privileges</strong></p></td><td><p>Built-in <code>clusterMonitor</code> and <code>read</code> on <code>admin</code>; no root or userAdmin roles</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Tailoring</strong></p></td><td><p>Company values from the register below override CIS defaults in the tailored audit file. Store it in <em>[repository / Tenable policy name]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Control register</h2>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">How to maintain this register</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><ul><li>One row per control. Control IDs are never renumbered or reused.</li><li><strong>Tenable Check</strong> describes what the audit item reads and its pass condition. Copy the CIS section from the audit item's <code>reference</code> field into <strong>CIS Reference</strong>.</li><li>Changing a Compliant Value is a policy change: record it in the change log and get approval.</li><li>After every scan, update Compliance % and Open CRITICAL / HIGH in the table at the top of the page.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Control ID</p></th><th><p>Control Name</p></th><th><p>Domain</p></th><th><p>Requirement</p></th><th><p>Severity</p></th><th><p>Compliant Value</p></th><th><p>Tenable Check (Audit / Query)</p></th><th><p>CIS Reference</p></th><th><p>Assessment</p></th><th><p>Last Review (Date / By)</p></th><th><p>Comments</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-VER-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Supported release with patches</p></td><td><p><code>VER</code></p></td><td><p>The server runs a MongoDB release that is not past end of life, at the latest patch level within the patch SLA.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>db.version()</code> in the approved version list</p></td><td><p><code>buildInfo</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-AAA-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Authorization enabled</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>Access control is on for every node. No node accepts unauthenticated connections.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>security.authorization: enabled</code></p></td><td><p>Unix audit: <code>mongod.conf</code>; database check: unauthenticated <code>listDatabases</code> fails</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-AAA-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Strong authentication mechanism</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>Users authenticate with SCRAM-SHA-256, x.509, LDAP or Kerberos. SCRAM-SHA-1 is not allowed.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>setParameter.authenticationMechanisms</code> excludes <code>SCRAM-SHA-1</code></p></td><td><p><code>getParameter: authenticationMechanisms</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-AAA-003</strong></p></td><td><p>Cluster member authentication</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>Replica set and shard members authenticate each other with x.509 certificates (keyFile only with an exception).</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>security.clusterAuthMode: x509</code></p></td><td><p>Unix audit: <code>mongod.conf</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-PRIV-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Least-privilege roles</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>root, userAdminAnyDatabase, dbOwner and clusterAdmin are granted only to approved administrators; applications use custom least-privilege roles.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Holders of the listed roles match the approved list</p></td><td><p><code>db.getSiblingDB('admin').system.users.find()</code> role listing</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>The reviewer compares role holders with the approved list.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-NET-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Bind to required interfaces only</p></td><td><p><code>NET</code></p></td><td><p>mongod listens only on localhost and the interfaces applications need.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>net.bindIp</code> does not contain <code>0.0.0.0</code> or <code>::</code>; <code>net.bindIpAll</code> not true</p></td><td><p>Unix audit: <code>mongod.conf</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-CRYPTO-001</strong></p></td><td><p>TLS required</p></td><td><p><code>CRYPTO</code></p></td><td><p>All client and intra-cluster connections use TLS 1.2 or higher.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>net.tls.mode: requireTLS</code>; <code>net.tls.disabledProtocols: TLS1_0,TLS1_1</code></p></td><td><p>Unix audit: <code>mongod.conf</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-CRYPTO-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Encryption at rest</p></td><td><p><code>CRYPTO</code></p></td><td><p>Databases classified Confidential or higher are encrypted at rest with keys held in KMIP / KMS.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>security.enableEncryption: true</code> with KMIP (Enterprise), or encrypted volumes (Community)</p></td><td><p>Unix audit: <code>mongod.conf</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Volume encryption is checked by the OS / storage team.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-SVC-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Server-side JavaScript disabled</p></td><td><p><code>SVC</code></p></td><td><p>Server-side JavaScript ($where, mapReduce JS, $function) is disabled unless an application needs it.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>security.javascriptEnabled: false</code></p></td><td><p>Unix audit: <code>mongod.conf</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-LOG-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Audit and system logging</p></td><td><p><code>LOG</code></p></td><td><p>Authentication, authorization failures and user / role changes are audited and the logs are forwarded to the SIEM.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>auditLog.destination</code> set (Enterprise / Percona); <code>systemLog.logAppend: true</code></p></td><td><p>Unix audit: <code>mongod.conf</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Community: forward systemLog to the SIEM and record an exception for missing audit events.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MONGO-OS-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Dedicated service account and file permissions</p></td><td><p><code>OS</code></p></td><td><p>mongod runs as a dedicated non-root account; keyFile and certificate keys are mode 600; dbPath is owned by the service account.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Process owner <code>mongod</code>; keyFile / PEM mode 600; dbPath mode 750 or stricter</p></td><td><p>Unix audit: process owner and file permission checks</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / 